WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.120
Good morning, Hank, it's Sunday. It's News Day. And I'm in an airport.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.860
Yay.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:08.340
[Intro music]

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.600
So Hank, a couple days ago, I was talking to a nerdfighter named Naomi

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.940
and she said that we should bring back the Evil Baby Orphanage

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.460
and I was like, "I don't know.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.860
Maybe the world doesn't need an Evil Baby Orphanage."

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.800
and then, North Korea launched a long-range missile into the ocean.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.500
Hank,

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.680
it's time to bring back the Evil Baby Orphanage.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.760
So as you know the evil baby orphanage is a fairly straightforward idea,

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.720
that was invented almost two years ago by a nerdfighter named Brooke,

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:35.180
as a way of resolving an argument that nerdfighters were having

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.980
over whether or not we should go back in time

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.860
and kill the evil baby Hitler.

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.340
Brooke came up with a compromise solution,

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.850
in which we would go back in time,

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:44.380
kidnap evil baby Hitler

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.340
and then take him to the Evil Baby Orphanage,

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:50.020
which would be a school designed explicitly for evil babies

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.600
in like Tibet or something.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.080
Well, Hank, I don't need to tell YOU

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.200
how good an idea the Evil Baby Orphanage is;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.540
the problem in the end wasn't that we found it difficult to build a time machine,

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:02.900
the problem was that you and I had a profound disagreement

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.440
over the nature of time travel paradoxes,

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.739
a disagreement which continues to this day, but Hank

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:10.420
I think it's time for us to put aside our petty squabble

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.000
because the world needs an Evil Baby Orphanage.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.500
Now, Hank, I know that it's tempting to say that North Korea launching a rocket into the ocean

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:17.669
isn't particularly impressive;

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:20.480
I could launch a rocket into the ocean if I wanted to.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:23.660
But Hank, there are a couple of important differences between North Korea and me.

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:28.600
First off. I'm not run by a crazy 68 year old Korean grandmother named Kim Jong-Il

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.000
What's that?

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.140
Really?

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:32.220
Are you sure?

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.200
Hank, I have some important breaking news:

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.460
Kim Jong-Il

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.100
is apparently a dude.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:37.780
But yeah, so first,

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:39.989
I'm not run by a crazy dude and second,

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.660
I don't have nuclear weapons.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.680
Even though the launch was what is technically known as

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:44.560
"an epic fail",

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:46.920
the international community is still really mad.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.500
Even China's mad.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.280
It's like when you go completely crazy and all your friends abandon you,

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:53.200
except for one friend who kind of stays with you

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.180
because she's also completely crazy,

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:56.760
and then finally she's like,

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:57.880
"Dear North Korea,

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:59.400
I love your totalitarianism,

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.800
and I think you've got an awesome cult of personality,

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.000
and it's great how you never let people leave your country

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.640
and you kill your political enemies.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.020
But come on!

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:08.200
WTF?

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.520
Best wishes,

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:10.500
China."

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.240
Now Hank, I'm not going to tell you that we need to get

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:14.140
Kim Jong-Il into the Evil Baby Orphanage;

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:15.610
he's just a fat crazy dude.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:19.240
We need to get his dead dad Kim Il-Sung into the Evil Baby Orphanage,

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.240
so that Kim Jong-Il never exists.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.100
Getting Kim Il-Sung into the Evil Baby Orphanage

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.680
would save literally millions of lives

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:27.300
and restore Korea to a single unified country.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.700
What? We'd have to build a time machine?

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.380
That- that shouldn't be a challenge.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.280
I mean,

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.360
nerdfighters do everything that we ask them to do.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:37.520
They ate 317 peeps for me,

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.620
you don't think they can build a time machine?

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:40.700
Get your head out of your ass.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:41.920
Sorry Hank, I don't mean to curse,

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:44.100
but this guy over here, telling me what nerdfighters can't do,

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.160
is really getting on my nerves.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:48.520
I mean, you call me when you built a pond sand filter in Bangladesh.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.060
Hank, you'll see me on Tuesday.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:52.740
[Singing] The people in the airport think that I'm crazy,

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:55.640
the people in the airport think that I'm crazy.

